.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 26, 2026
.Dt PASSWD 1
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm passwd
.Nd change a user's password
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility changes a user's password: the caller's own, or, for the
superuser only, that of
.Ar user .
.Pp
The change goes through the
.Dq passwd
PAM policy in
.Pa /etc/pam.d/passwd .
A user other than the superuser is first asked for their current
password.
The new password is asked for twice, hashed with SHA-512, and stored in
.Pa /etc/master.passwd ,
after which
.Pa /etc/passwd
is regenerated as by
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8 .
Changing the password clears any change time set for the account.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/master.passwd -compact
.It Pa /etc/master.passwd
the account database
.It Pa /etc/passwd
its public form
.It Pa /etc/pam.d/passwd
the PAM policy
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr crypt 3 ,
.Xr pam.conf 5 ,
.Xr passwd 5 ,
.Xr pwd_mkdb 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.At v6 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
.Sh BUGS
.Nm
must run as the superuser to write the account files, and OxideBSD does
not yet honor the set-user-ID bit, so only the superuser can use it.
